.TH DANBY-GONORRHEA 1
.SH NAME
danby-gonorrhea \- two-sex SIS transmission model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/gonorrhea
.SH MODEL
Sw'=-bm Sw Im+gw Iw; Iw'=bm Sw Im-gw Iw;
Sm'=-bw Sm Iw+gm Im; Im'=bw Sm Iw-gm Im.
.PP
Recovery returns individuals to susceptibility, so immunity does not accumulate.
Separate transmission and recovery parameters expose asymmetric prevalence in
the two interacting groups.
.SH DISPLAY
Four histories show susceptible and infectious fractions for women and men.
Each pair is conserved independently and that invariant is regression-tested.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag any compartment bar.  Tracks set both directional transmission rates and
both recovery rates.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/gonorrhea.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/gonorrhea.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR populationmodel (2),
.IR danby-crossinfection (1)
